# Polymarket-sharps schedule (Debian Chromebook, always-on). Install with:
#     crontab scripts/crontab.example
# and remove with `crontab -r`. Inspect with `crontab -l`. All output goes to
# data/cron.log (gitignored; rotated nightly by recompute.sh).
#
# Cadence rationale (see DECISIONS.md):
#   - ingest every 5 min: the global /trades feed only serves the most recent
#     ~10k platform-wide trades with no time filter, so polls must OVERLAP or
#     trades fall in the gap permanently. One 10k poll spans ~5-10 min of feed.
#     To hold that cadence, ingest only APPENDS its rows to a small delta parquet
#     part (~1 min/tick) instead of rewriting the multi-million-row ledger, which
#     took 5-8 min and made every other tick skip on the lock (DECISIONS.md
#     "Fixes (2026-07-23)").
#   - recompute nightly: fold-delta + backfill + features/validate/rank/report.
#     features peaks ~3 GB RSS, so it runs once a night, off the ingest cadence's
#     back. The fold is its first step, so every stage below reads a full ledger.
#
# Concurrency safety: ingest and backfill are ledger writers guarded by a shared
# flock (data/interim/.ledger.lock). ingest uses -n and SKIPS a tick if the
# nightly backfill holds the lock; backfill blocks until any in-flight ingest
# finishes. So the two writers never run at once (writes are atomic anyway, so a
# skip/kill costs a re-run, never corruption). The read-only pipeline stages run
# unlocked. Absolute paths so cron's minimal environment resolves them.

*/5 *  * * *  /home/agent47/polymarket-sharps/scripts/ingest.sh
17  3  * * *  /home/agent47/polymarket-sharps/scripts/recompute.sh

# --- Project 3 forward scoring (read-only) ---
# Re-fetches each frozen cohort's post-freeze trades and scores whether the
# cohort beats its frozen baseline on bets placed after the freeze. Public GETs
# only. Every 2 days: sports resolves in hours-days, forecasters in weeks.
# 37 5 */2 * *  /home/agent47/polymarket-sharps/scripts/forward_score.sh
